          <h2>A commuter town with an office-park core</h2>
          <p>Westhill is best known as home to Prime Four Business Park and a cluster of other energy-sector office developments, alongside its role as a place where a large number of residents commute into Aberdeen for work. That combination shapes the kind of breakdown we see here: a good proportion happen either at the start or end of the working day, as vehicles that have sat overnight or all day are asked to start again, or as commuters head out onto the A944 into slower-moving traffic.</p>

          <h2>Business-park recovery</h2>
          <p>If you break down at Prime Four or one of Westhill's other business parks, the layout can involve multiple car parks, service roads and building entrances, so the site name and building number help us a great deal. These call-outs often need to be handled with minimum fuss during a working day — we treat business-park recovery the same way whether it's one car in a quiet corner of the car park or a vehicle blocking a thoroughfare.</p>

          <h2>The road out to Alford and Deeside</h2>
          <p>Westhill also sits on the route many drivers use heading further west towards Alford and the wider Donside and Deeside areas. If your breakdown happens on this stretch rather than in the town itself, let us know your direction of travel and any nearby villages or junctions — the road narrows and becomes more rural the further west you go, which affects how we plan the recovery.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Commuting into or out of Westhill?</strong> A flat battery after a car has sat in an office car park all day is one of the most common calls we get here. If your car won't start at the end of the working day, get yourself somewhere safe and give us a call — we'll talk through what's happened and get moving.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

